{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction","id":1555955,"title":"Would this be an interesting premise for a Hunter fanfiction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-29T12:26:30-08:00","id":1555955,"title":"Would this be an interesting premise for a Hunter fanfiction?","content":"The premise is that a Hunter before their imbuing had a Girlfriend but after his Imbuing he hesitated to see her again for a while due to distancing himself from others but when they finally meet up again that's when he discovers his Girlfriend was a Werewolf the entire time. This results in a heartbreaking discussion where his Girlfriend leaves due to him not trusting her. Sometime later the Hunter's cell discovers the existence of Pentex after digging too deep into the existence of &quot;mutants&quot; they end up having a First Team sent after them which leads to a skirmish before they're suddenly rescued by a Garou pack led by his ex-girlfriend who still loved him. After explanations he makes up with his Girlfriend again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 11-29-2025, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T14:22:51-08:00","id":1555957,"title":"","content":"It's fanfic... there's always going to be people down for starcrossed lovers overcoming &quot;fate&quot; and romance winning over the base assumptions of the setting.<br /> <br /> As a fan of both WtA and HtR? Not interesting at all. It's the WoD. Love doesn't conquer all. The Garou and the Imbued are not on the same page and no matter how hard they try, an Imbued and a Garou are going to be pulled apart by their social groups and supernatural natures. HtR: Moonstruck, like the rest of the &quot;enemy&quot; books in the line, have fairly good sections discussing all the pitfalls of crossover relationships for the Imbued.<br /> <br /> This is a setting were a Wayward could show up at any moment and force the Imbued cells into fighting the pack because the Wayward is never going to accept such tolerance of monsters by a cell; either the tainted cell dies, or the monsters die and the Imbued see the flaw in their moral compromise. The Wayward &quot;wins&quot; either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T14:49:08-08:00","id":1555958,"title":"","content":"Meh, you guys are hard to please. But yes, their meetings would probably be limited and he'd probably warn his Girlfriend about Waywards and other Zealots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T15:45:23-08:00","id":1555959,"title":"","content":"I'm not that hard to please? I've just seen hundreds of versions of this plot-line before, so it's not interesting to me. It wasn't really that interesting when HtR came out in the first place because gothic romance and urban fantasy genre pieces were chocked full of these sorts of stories. White Wolf sued the makers of the movie Underworld for doing a vampire x werewolf version of this.<br /> <br /> You asked if it's interesting. It's not to me, because you're competing with decades of previous attempts at core plot. I'm sure there are people that can innovate and do new takes that might be worth it if given a shot... but there's a point where it's also on them to pitch something novel to an audience that's heard the core-plot pitch hundreds of times already. I referenced a line from <i>Shakespeare</i> in my previous post, because that's how well trod these kinds of stories are in English culture.<br /> <br /> I'm also just one guy. You don't need my permission to write whatever fanfic you want. I'm not someone that's active on popular fanfic sites reviewing works, so you don't have to worry about me slamming this in those spaces or something. If you want to write it, write it. But if you want my opinion? My opinion is that it's not interesting. It's not in keeping with the tone of the WoD, and it's exceptionally overdone within the relevant genres, so I need a much more intriguing hook to feel otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T15:55:53-08:00","id":1555960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1555958#post1555958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, you guys are hard to please. But yes, their meetings would probably be limited and he'd probably warn his Girlfriend about Waywards and other Zealots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the WoD is just the victim of continual sabotage when it comes to crossover. A run of 14 years, and 14 years spent making each character type hellbent on trying to kill the others. When it doesn't have cracked out &quot;official&quot; fiction, anyway (Crinos-born getting Imbued women pregnant! Garou who are also Bastet via the Progenitors! Mass hysteria!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T16:29:54-08:00","id":1555961,"title":"","content":"What was that last part about Metis getting women pregnant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T16:34:33-08:00","id":1555962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1555959#post1555959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not that hard to please? I've just seen hundreds of versions of this plot-line before, so it's not interesting to me. It wasn't really that interesting when HtR came out in the first place because gothic romance and urban fantasy genre pieces were chocked full of these sorts of stories. White Wolf sued the makers of the movie Underworld for doing a vampire x werewolf version of this.<br /> <br /> You asked if it's interesting. It's not to me, because you're competing with decades of previous attempts at core plot. I'm sure there are people that can innovate and do new takes that might be worth it if given a shot... but there's a point where it's also on them to pitch something novel to an audience that's heard the core-plot pitch hundreds of times already. I referenced a line from <i>Shakespeare</i> in my previous post, because that's how well trod these kinds of stories are in English culture.<br /> <br /> I'm also just one guy. You don't need my permission to write whatever fanfic you want. I'm not someone that's active on popular fanfic sites reviewing works, so you don't have to worry about me slamming this in those spaces or something. If you want to write it, write it. But if you want my opinion? My opinion is that it's not interesting. It's not in keeping with the tone of the WoD, and it's exceptionally overdone within the relevant genres, so I need a much more intriguing hook to feel otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I did mention distrust from the Hunter after the discovery which is different from most stories and the trust having to be earned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T17:04:48-08:00","id":1555965,"title":"","content":"It really isn't that special of a plot point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T21:52:10-08:00","id":1555969,"title":"","content":"While I echo both previous posters, that this is an extremely overdone plot and that WoD sabotaged itself time and again against crossover, I actually think you should go for it!<br /> <br /> You won't easily please most of us because most of us have been around for quite some time and seen a lot. I have more time as a Storyteller than some RPG Youtubers have of life.<br /> <br /> But you don't have to please us, you have to have fun and experiences. Most of us wouldn't be easily pleased by our own past selves, either, by the way.<br /> <br /> Fanfiction also isn't the focus of those forums, so most of us aren't the target-audience for this idea. Not that you shouldn't ask here, but you should also ask in fanfic forums. And you should go forth and write this, it's not a new idea, but it's not a bad one, either. You'll get valuable experience and valuable feedback from readers, and most important have fun doing it.<br /> <br /> A key difference from this to your previous threads about characters is that in those threads you had already made the characters, regardless of what we said about them. I'd like to see a new post here in the future with the actual link for the story, or at least a more or less complete draft. In the meanwhile you may ask about minor details as you do it. And never let our hardened opinions get in the way of your fun, no one here want's to make you give up or stop having fun with the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T07:33:08-08:00","id":1555979,"title":"","content":"I also thought about an entire sub-plot where the Hunter cell discovers the Pentex Conspiracy and find out about the existence of a Ferectoi who they think is the &quot;anti-christ&quot; to give the story some intrigue and mild humor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T10:53:13-08:00","id":1555980,"title":"","content":"But I have thought of some details for the story, all he knew at first about his Girlfriend was that she was a hippie and that she had the strange name of Crying-Wolf and acted a bit weird, but he figured that it was probably just hippie culture or something. Then after his Imbuing he chose to isolate himself due to being concerned for his loved ones' safety like most Hunters, then his Girlfriend called him because she hadn't seen him in a while to which he responds he's been having a rough time. This causes her to visit him bringing a gift, this is when he finds out through the Second Sight that she isn't human much to his despair.<br /> <br /> He thinks to himself, &quot;No, not her too.&quot;<br /> <br /> He then asks, &quot;You're one of them aren't you?&quot;<br /> <br /> She's taken aback at this question, &quot;What do you mean?&quot;<br /> <br /> This leads to the confession that she's a werewolf. Where he then asks her how many people she killed.<br /> <br /> She's shocked by the question but then answers with shame that she lost count but clarifies that they were evil people.<br /> <br /> The Hunter responds coldly saying, &quot;And why should I believe that?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T13:35:03-08:00","id":1555995,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, there's the Curse and Primal Instinct.<br /> <br /> Werewolves in human form still feel like &quot;savage&quot; in some way, which can be both repelling and alluring.<br /> <br /> Do with it what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T15:02:27-08:00","id":1556003,"title":"","content":"As much as it might matter, while Second Sight is active, the Curse and Animal Magnetism really shouldn't apply to an Imbued. Second Sight can be a problem in cooperative crossover because it denies large categories of powers from working on the Imbued; they don't get to be selective and let powers that would be beneficial to them through.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> To a bigger literary issue, I'm curious:<br /> <br /> Samuelalpha86, what is the difference for you between writing fanfic, and writing original stories in an TTRPG setting? Fanfic generally focuses and more traditional literary settings, and thus fanfic communities have strong positive feelings towards taking major liberties with the core assumptions of the original to explore new approaches to established characters and settings. TTRPGs are settings designed for people to create their own stories within. While not as common these days as it feels like it used to be, writing your own in-setting stories for RPGs used to be more like solo-play RPGs where there's a higher expectation of keeping to the core conceits of the setting even if for whatever reason you're not telling a story with friends and dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T16:54:30-08:00","id":1556011,"title":"","content":"Well, what I said was that he met his werewolf girlfriend before his Imbuing.<br /> <br /> writing a fanfic means it's not an official publication; it's a fan work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:13:59-08:00","id":1556012,"title":"","content":"So, are you saying that from your perspective there is no difference? Because I think you'd find that most fanfic communities would feel very differently. I feel like you're edging towards the etymological fallacy, which is where your definition is based on the historical roots of a word/phrase (&quot;fan&quot; and &quot;fiction&quot;) in a fashion that doesn't acknowledge the contemporary usage of the word/phrase as having a different or more specific meaning. This can lead to a lot of miscommunication in what your intentions for the story are, and what goals you might have in its construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:25:41-08:00","id":1556014,"title":"","content":"Fanfiction-fiction written by a fan of, and featuring characters from, a particular TV series, film, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:36:36-08:00","id":1556015,"title":"","content":"Are you familiar with After Action Report fiction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:38:17-08:00","id":1556017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction#post1555955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After explanations he makes up with his Girlfriend again.</div> </div> </div> </div>To offer some more pointed advice: Take this bit at the very end... Why does this happen?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:40:37-08:00","id":1556018,"title":"","content":"I only heard of it now, but doesn't that involve strategic analysis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:41:59-08:00","id":1556019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556017#post1556017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To offer some more pointed advice: Take this bit at the very end... Why does this happen?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why does he make up with her again? Because she saved him, which meant he could trust her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:45:05-08:00","id":1556020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556019#post1556019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does he make up with her again? Because she saved him, which meant he could trust her.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why did she save him? He didn't trust her, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:49:57-08:00","id":1556021,"title":"","content":"She still loved him even though he broke her heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:51:23-08:00","id":1556022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556021#post1556021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She still loved him even though he broke her heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. But why, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T18:04:09-08:00","id":1556023,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I guess she understood that werewolves have a bad reputation, so she was more forgiving. She also really liked him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T18:17:05-08:00","id":1556025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556023#post1556023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I guess she understood that werewolves have a bad reputation, so she was more forgiving. She also really liked him.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then why does he make up with her again at the end? Wouldn't it be the other way around? The Hunter-guy's distrustful and abruptly ends the relationship but she's the understanding one and is forgiving. Seems like she likes him more than he likes her. Also, looking at it like that, isn't she doing more in this story than he does? Your male Hunter-protagonist is just kinda around as plot happens around him. And then it's a victory that the Hunter-guy forgives (?) his girlfriend for being a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T18:19:47-08:00","id":1556026,"title":"","content":"It's more that she regains his trust and he apologizes for not trusting her. He was just being understandably cautious being a monster hunter and all that, he only saw monsters as murderers but after seeing how loyal she was he figured she couldn't have lied to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T18:36:19-08:00","id":1556027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556026#post1556026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more that she regains his trust and he apologizes for not trusting her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, so you want the story to be about a loser-protagonist who breaks up with a person who's way cooler than him. But it's okay, because this person (somehow) is still in love with the loser and therefore none of the protagonist's actions have consequences. More than that, the moment when all hope is lost, the girlfriend that has been cast aside returns and saves the protagonist! And it's only now, after service rendered, the protagonist remembers there's value to this person called &quot;girlfriend&quot; in his life. But hey, it's all &quot;water under the bridge&quot; or something - and now they're together again. <br /> <br /> Sounds like a terrible story, to be honest...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T18:47:39-08:00","id":1556028,"title":"","content":"Hey, he's not a loser for being cautious he still loved her, think of it from his perspective imagine finding out that someone you loved and trusted turned out to be a Serial Killer as far as you knew. Also, it's not that his actions don't have consequences it's just that his Girlfriend was understanding and compassionate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:00:24-08:00","id":1556030,"title":"","content":"&quot;Understanding and compassionate&quot; are descriptions, not explanations. The girlfriend-character still feels underwritten. Right now, I picture a roomba (on cleanup-duty!) when you talk about this guy's &quot;girlfriend&quot;. That's how alive she seems. And maybe your protagonist likes to talk to roombas but that's what we're working with here, right now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:07:25-08:00","id":1556031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556018#post1556018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only heard of it now, but doesn't that involve strategic analysis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the &quot;fiction&quot; part is what separates it from military after action reports.<br /> <br /> Back in the early days of wargames, TTRPGs, and 4X games, due to the association with military terminology, used the phrase AAR to refer to fiction based on game-play; though eventually it expanded from direct dramatization of actual play to include games that could have been.<br /> <br /> The important distinctions between AAR fics and fanfics, is as I mentioned. The AAR fics focus on what could happen in a game (whether actually played, or imagined), where fanfic focuses on innovating on existing settings/characters. Which you're aiming to do impacts a lot of how to think about where to take a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:13:12-08:00","id":1556032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556030#post1556030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Understanding and compassionate&quot; are descriptions, not explanations. The girlfriend-character still feels underwritten. Right now, I picture a roomba (on cleanup-duty!) when you talk about this guy's &quot;girlfriend&quot;. That's how alive she seems. And maybe your protagonist likes to talk to roombas but that's what we're working with here, right now.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh just shut up, I haven't gotten that far in writing the story yet. Also, it is an explanation, I explained clearly that werewolves are known for killing people so he would be understandably distrusting which she would understand and clearly you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:30:10-08:00","id":1556033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556032#post1556032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh just shut up, I haven't gotten that far in writing the story yet. Also, I explained clearly that werewolves are known for killing people so he would be understandably distrusting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, here we go... &quot;I haven't gotten that far in writing the story yet&quot;. So why are you here, frankly? Let me tell you what your progress on your so-called story is: It's 0%. Why you would wanna make a thread about a story with 0% progress beats me... <br /> <br /> And so that's how I responded: I see a story-pitch with 0% progress and the best thing to do, I think, is to make said person realise they're at 0%. <br /> <br /> You're still at 0%, mind you. <br /> <br /> How do I know that, you may wonder... Well, there hasn't been a single moment when you said or described something that felt inspired. You're grasping at straws. Always. <br /> <br /> You will know the difference when inspiration actually strikes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:35:02-08:00","id":1556034,"title":"","content":"I said it was a premise for a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:39:29-08:00","id":1556035,"title":"","content":"Also, in case you haven't noticed by now she's a Child of Gaia named Crying-Wolf. I didn't state this yet but she's a Philodox and a Metis. The Hunter is a Hermit with Aspergers Syndrome who is very pop-culture savvy and likes to make jokes, which I also didn't mention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 11-30-2025, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:52:48-08:00","id":1556036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556034#post1556034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said it was a premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, don't make me laugh again! <br /> <br /> Look around! Have at least some sense of decorum! You see a lot of threads on here talking about so-called &quot;premises&quot;?! <br /> <br /> If you had actually written the blasted story you were talking about, I would be kinder but to make a thread about &quot;you merely thinking to write it at some point&quot;... Ha! And this would be the first piece of fiction you would present on this forum as well. Also, this forum shouldn't be your sounding-board for your dumb ideas. Just write the flipping story and let us read it. It may be shit - and that's okay. You're starting out on a difficult path (for many reasons). So just write the goddamn thing. Take the criticism - and do better next time. <br /> <br /> You're also not gonna get better by not writing it.<br /> <br /> But what you're doing right now... Stop hedging, just sit down and write the fucking story in your head. And if that fucking story isn't there in your head, you should think about that instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T19:55:45-08:00","id":1556038,"title":"","content":"Quit being a bitch! I'm thinking of how to go about it, writing takes time. You're only giving me more reasons to hate you because you're being nothing but a disrespectful, rude piece of shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 11-30-2025, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T20:09:57-08:00","id":1556042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556038#post1556038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quit being a bitch! I'm thinking of how to go about it, writing takes time. You're only giving me more reasons to hate you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on, who started the thread... Oh wait, that was you... Sorry for responding to your thread of &quot;Samuel wants to hear everybody's opinion!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Writing takes time&quot;... Well, apparently not as much as it took you to make a thread on this forum about your yet un-produced writing... That writing seemed to have happened quite fast...<br /> <br /> <b>Just write the story.</b> It doesn't matter how good or bad it is. Let's start from there rather than this theoretical limbo-state of talking about a text that maybe someday may exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T20:24:11-08:00","id":1556043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556035#post1556035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in case you haven't noticed by now she's a Child of Gaia named Crying-Wolf. I didn't state this yet but she's a Philodox and a Metis. The Hunter is a Hermit with Aspergers Syndrome who is very pop-culture savvy and likes to make jokes, which I also didn't mention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's really helping. A Metis, even a Child of Gaia, risks turning into Crinos when they're unconscious (many people don't count normal sleep as a house rule, but in most editions the RAW are that you need a Gift/Merit/Fetish/etc. or sleep counts as falling unconscious for reverting to Breed form). And Metis that spend time with humans tend to be given a more human sounding name. Metis might find some comfort in a relationship with a normal human (if they can manage the Rage and Curse and all that) as they're not going to be judged as much as they would be in Garou society and of course aren't going to be allowed to take a fertile mate in Garou society, it's still a source of problems since sterility can be a major source of stress in relationships and stress in relationships lead to Frenzy checks.<br /> <br /> On his side, having a significant ASD diagnosis only makes the avoiding of stress Frenzies harder (if it was from before his Imbuing, he'd have an additional Derangement after only complicating that further, and if it's from after as his Derangement it would make a sudden radical change in his ability to socialize with her), along with him Imbuing as a Hermit means being near her for extending periods of time nearly impossible. Even at Tolerance 5 a Hermit can only endure the Static for 5 hours before the pain kicks in and starts to dish out penalties... and Hermits generally need to work on Tolerance in play as it's not a freebie to help with their situation on Imbuing as a mercy from the Messengers. They're called Hermits for a reason. The Static is always on, always active, always pushing them to insanity, and it only gets worse around both the Imbued and the supernatural.<br /> <br /> You are giving yourself a huge task by adding even more barriers than &quot;Hunter dating monster&quot; already has... it seems counterproductive. We all have our own ways to plotting out a story, but the more &quot;drama&quot; creep you let get in at the early stages, the more work you're making for yourself before you even get into the actual writing part.<br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> And while I do agree that Knightingale is being overly harsh about all this... I can also understand her frustrations. You post a lot as if you want feedback, but then get extremely defensive towards feedback that isn't positive. Name calling and cussing isn't making anyone look good, but it's also frustrating for us to try to help you and be treated pretty poorly for it. If you want help and advice... listen even if it's not what you were initially hoping for. Otherwise people are just going to stop trying to help. Either by ignoring you, or by just being terse and dismissive in response.<br /> <br /> Seriously. Take a look at your posting history. How many threads like this have you started? How many do you have something to show for it? How many have you communicated that to the thread that it was helpful and you've made significant progress? Can you see why it's not so unreasonable for someone to respond with the advice of, &quot;stop talking about things and start doing them.&quot; It's not exactly uncommon advice in many aspects of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T21:26:14-08:00","id":1556045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556043#post1556043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And while I do agree that Knightingale is being overly harsh about all this... I can also understand her frustrations. You post a lot as if you want feedback, but then get extremely defensive towards feedback that isn't positive. Name calling and cussing isn't making anyone look good, but it's also frustrating for us to try to help you and be treated pretty poorly for it. If you want help and advice... listen even if it's not what you were initially hoping for. Otherwise people are just going to stop trying to help. Either by ignoring you, or by just being terse and dismissive in response.<br /> <br /> Seriously. Take a look at your posting history. How many threads like this have you started? How many do you have something to show for it? How many have you communicated that to the thread that it was helpful and you've made significant progress? Can you see why it's not so unreasonable for someone to respond with the advice of, &quot;stop talking about things and start doing them.&quot; It's not exactly uncommon advice in many aspects of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I know, the cussing and all that... Not that great. But I'm just seeing you talk with this guy day in and day out and it doesn't seem to make a difference! And you are offering sensible advice! <br /> <br /> But I thought &quot;Let's try something else. Maybe this will get through to him.&quot;. Just being mean in the other thread wasn't enough. So I thought doing a &quot;mean mother&quot;-routine would make a difference. You know, mixing sensible advice with demands and harsh, vulgar language. He called me a bitch - so that's a change, I guess.<br /> <br /> I'm a He/Him btw. But it's okay. At least, this approach got some response, I guess. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, it's just about figuring out how you can get Samuel to get anywhere with what he has proposed he wants to do...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T01:14:39-08:00","id":1556047,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the pronouns... it's kinda hard to tell most of the time and I couldn't remember if you had posted anything in the past. Plus you were successful in doing some mom energy :P<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the larger point you're trying to make is wrong... and I'm not such a hypocrite to say you're over a line in getting harsh here. IMO the Internet wildly devalues expressing negative emotions to the detriment of our ability to talk to each other like human beings. If you're polite about it, expressing frustration/etc. seemed to be ignored or treated as a weakness to be attacked, and if you just start punctuating with some profanity you become the bad guy as if being the first to let civility slip a bit is the worst crime possible in text. I have yet to find any sort of middle-ground where I can feel reliably heard in such things and avoid causing a fuss at the same time.<br /> <br /> I'm also sympathetic to Samuel in all this because I remember what it's like to have a lot of ideas and struggle with trying to make any of them happen, and having a lot of people try to help but it never being the help I needed. And they had less excuses because this was in person where communication or direct examples are a lot easier to do than online only conversations. Sometimes I eventually got it to click and figured out how to start working all that help in after getting over the block... and sometimes I just had to humble up and acknowledge particular thing was never going to be an artistic outlet for me.<br /> <br /> But as the people that are trying to help, I don't want to say someone else is hopeless at something, so the best I can do is try until they figure out what they want to do in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T02:20:19-08:00","id":1556051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556003#post1556003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as it might matter, while Second Sight is active, the Curse and Animal Magnetism really shouldn't apply to an Imbued.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I was thinking about their relationship before the Imbuing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28613\" data-vbnamecard=\"28613\">Samuelalpha86</a>, the best thing you do is still to write the story, however it comes to you. Don't worry about perfection or about what people will think.<br /> <br /> First times aren't for good results, they're for a fun process. Even accomplished writers, what you see published is their best works, not their actual first stories, those were terrible more often than not, but <i>writing them was fun</i>. Most things you'll only get good at by doing when you're not yet good at them.<br /> <br /> Before that getting more and more advice will only overwhelm you. I still remember how much I tried to learn and take in every advice I could before running a game, and how much it actually paralyzed me instead of helping, because it was a lot in my head without the context I actually needed. My first games were a mess of me trying to plan ahead everything just to end up improvising a lot of BS because I didn't prepared for what would actually happen and forgot most things when I needed them.<br /> <br /> Wanting to do good only gets in the way. You seem to already know what you want to write, you don't have to defend your ideas or get validation for them. After you have something written we can discuss, comment, like or dislike, and you'll have a better grasp of the basics to actually give this advice context.<br /> <br /> After writing it you can even try your hand at writing the reverse version (the story from the POV of the other character), or the Gender-Bender version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T08:08:13-08:00","id":1556061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1555955-would-this-be-an-interesting-premise-for-a-hunter-fanfiction?p=1556043#post1556043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that's really helping. A Metis, even a Child of Gaia, risks turning into Crinos when they're unconscious (many people don't count normal sleep as a house rule, but in most editions the RAW are that you need a Gift/Merit/Fetish/etc. or sleep counts as falling unconscious for reverting to Breed form). And Metis that spend time with humans tend to be given a more human sounding name. Metis might find some comfort in a relationship with a normal human (if they can manage the Rage and Curse and all that) as they're not going to be judged as much as they would be in Garou society and of course aren't going to be allowed to take a fertile mate in Garou society, it's still a source of problems since sterility can be a major source of stress in relationships and stress in relationships lead to Frenzy checks.<br /> <br /> On his side, having a significant ASD diagnosis only makes the avoiding of stress Frenzies harder (if it was from before his Imbuing, he'd have an additional Derangement after only complicating that further, and if it's from after as his Derangement it would make a sudden radical change in his ability to socialize with her), along with him Imbuing as a Hermit means being near her for extending periods of time nearly impossible. Even at Tolerance 5 a Hermit can only endure the Static for 5 hours before the pain kicks in and starts to dish out penalties... and Hermits generally need to work on Tolerance in play as it's not a freebie to help with their situation on Imbuing as a mercy from the Messengers. They're called Hermits for a reason. The Static is always on, always active, always pushing them to insanity, and it only gets worse around both the Imbued and the supernatural.<br /> <br /> You are giving yourself a huge task by adding even more barriers than &quot;Hunter dating monster&quot; already has... it seems counterproductive. We all have our own ways to plotting out a story, but the more &quot;drama&quot; creep you let get in at the early stages, the more work you're making for yourself before you even get into the actual writing part.<br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> And while I do agree that Knightingale is being overly harsh about all this... I can also understand her frustrations. You post a lot as if you want feedback, but then get extremely defensive towards feedback that isn't positive. Name calling and cussing isn't making anyone look good, but it's also frustrating for us to try to help you and be treated pretty poorly for it. If you want help and advice... listen even if it's not what you were initially hoping for. Otherwise people are just going to stop trying to help. Either by ignoring you, or by just being terse and dismissive in response.<br /> <br /> Seriously. Take a look at your posting history. How many threads like this have you started? How many do you have something to show for it? How many have you communicated that to the thread that it was helpful and you've made significant progress? Can you see why it's not so unreasonable for someone to respond with the advice of, &quot;stop talking about things and start doing them.&quot; It's not exactly uncommon advice in many aspects of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she probably didn't spend the night with him to avoid changing to Crinos in her sleep. Although they probably still had sex a few times. Also, the reason I chose that he had Aspergers Syndrome before his Imbuing was because I felt that would fit the criteria for a Hermit, since they'd already be socially withdrawn and reluctant to endanger themselves in the first place. Most of the time he acts as the &quot;Man behind the Chair&quot; for his cell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-01-2025, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T14:15:20-08:00","id":1556068,"title":"","content":"Although I didn't say this before, I did make a short-series of one-shot stories about the World of Darkness a while back.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/14397718/1/Tales-from-The-World-of-Darkness\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1439771...ld-of-Darkness</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 12-01-2025, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}